{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/sse/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Diffence Bio"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"61e49219-b081-5310-97fe-5fcc538d5f66","excerpt":". SSE (Server-Sent Events) Protocol and AI Large Model Chat 1. Introduction In AI large model chat applications, achieving real-time, streaming responses is…","html":"<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 1000px; width: 100%; margin: 2em 0;\"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/cecd0/ai.jpg\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 56.400000000000006%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/jpeg;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"network\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/a2510/ai.jpg\"\n        srcset=\"/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/0479a/ai.jpg 250w,\n/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/41099/ai.jpg 500w,\n/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/a2510/ai.jpg 1000w,\n/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/c58a3/ai.jpg 1500w,\n/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/3acf0/ai.jpg 2000w,\n/static/327c77709c4a738f14628aebf0bc909b/cecd0/ai.jpg 5120w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 1000px) 100vw, 1000px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span>.</p>\n<h1>SSE (Server-Sent Events) Protocol and AI Large Model Chat</h1>\n<h2>1. Introduction</h2>\n<p>In AI large model chat applications, achieving real-time, streaming responses is crucial for enhancing user experience. Common technical solutions include WebSocket, SSE (Server-Sent Events), and polling. Among them, SSE, as a lightweight one-way communication protocol, is particularly suitable for streaming responses in AI-generated conversations.</p>\n<p>This article introduces the working principles of SSE, how to use SSE for streaming transmission in AI large model chats, and provides sample code.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>2. Overview of the SSE Protocol</h2>\n<p>SSE (Server-Sent Events) is an HTTP-based server push technology primarily used for servers to push real-time data to clients. Unlike WebSocket, SSE only supports one-way communication from the server to the client and is based on HTTP/1.1 persistent connections.</p>\n<h3>2.1 Key Features of SSE</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>One-way communication</strong>: The server actively pushes data to the client.</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP-based</strong>: No additional protocols required, compatible with HTTP/2.</li>\n<li><strong>Automatic reconnection</strong>: Clients support automatic reconnection after disconnection.</li>\n<li><strong>Lightweight</strong>: Compared to WebSocket, SSE is simpler and consumes fewer resources.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2.2 Comparison Between SSE and WebSocket</h3>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Feature</th>\n<th>SSE</th>\n<th>WebSocket</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Connection</td>\n<td>HTTP persistent connection</td>\n<td>Full-duplex TCP connection</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Communication Direction</td>\n<td>Server → Client (One-way)</td>\n<td>Client ↔ Server (Bidirectional)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Compatibility</td>\n<td>Compatible with HTTP/2, easy to use</td>\n<td>Requires additional protocol support</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Auto-reconnect</td>\n<td>Built-in support</td>\n<td>Requires manual implementation</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Use Cases</td>\n<td>Streaming push, event notifications</td>\n<td>Real-time chat, gaming communication</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr>\n<h2>3. Application in AI Large Model Chat</h2>\n<p>AI large models (such as ChatGPT, Gemini) typically use <strong>streaming output</strong>, where text is generated word by word or sentence by sentence, enhancing interactive experience.</p>\n<p>SSE is well-suited for such scenarios, allowing the frontend to receive AI-generated text in real-time without waiting for a complete response.</p>\n<h3>3.1 Server-side Implementation (Using Python FastAPI)</h3>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"python\"><pre class=\"language-python\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> fastapi <span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> FastAPI\n<span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> fastapi<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>responses <span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> StreamingResponse\n<span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> time\n\napp <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> FastAPI<span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"token function\">ai_stream</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span>\n    messages <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Hello\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">\" this\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">\" is\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">\" an\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">\" AI\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token string\">\" response\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">for</span> msg <span class=\"token keyword\">in</span> messages<span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">yield</span> <span class=\"token string-interpolation\"><span class=\"token string\">f\"data: </span><span class=\"token interpolation\"><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>msg<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span></span><span class=\"token string\">\\n\\n\"</span></span>\n        time<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>sleep<span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token number\">0.5</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"token decorator annotation punctuation\">@app<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>get</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"/chat\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span>\n<span class=\"token keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"token function\">chat_stream</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">:</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> StreamingResponse<span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>ai_stream<span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> media_type<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"text/event-stream\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span></code></pre></div>\n<h3>3.2 Client-side Implementation (Using JavaScript Fetch API)</h3>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> eventSource <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">EventSource</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"/chat\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\neventSource<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function-variable function\">onmessage</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">event</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Received:\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> event<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>data<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\neventSource<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function-variable function\">onerror</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">error</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Connection lost, attempting to reconnect...\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<h3>3.3 Parsing SSE Text Format in the Frontend</h3>\n<p>SSE messages follow a simple text format, where each message is prefixed with <code class=\"language-text\">data:</code> and ends with a double newline (<code class=\"language-text\">\\n\\n</code>). The frontend needs to properly parse these messages to extract meaningful content. Below is an enhanced example:</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"javascript\"><pre class=\"language-javascript\"><code class=\"language-javascript\"><span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> eventSource <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">EventSource</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"/chat\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\neventSource<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function-variable function\">onmessage</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">event</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> messages <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> event<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>data<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">split</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"\\n\\n\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">map</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">msg</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> msg<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">trim</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">filter</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">msg</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> msg<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    \n    messages<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">forEach</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">parsedData</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Received message:\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> parsedData<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        \n        <span class=\"token comment\">// Append the received message to a chat UI</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> chatBox <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> document<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">getElementById</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"chat-box\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token keyword\">if</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>chatBox<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n            <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> messageElement <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> document<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">createElement</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"p\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n            messageElement<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span>textContent <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> parsedData<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n            chatBox<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">appendChild</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>messageElement<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\neventSource<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function-variable function\">onerror</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token parameter\">error</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">error</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"SSE connection error:\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> error<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    eventSource<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">close</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token function\">setTimeout</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token operator\">=></span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n        console<span class=\"token punctuation\">.</span><span class=\"token function\">log</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Reconnecting...\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n        eventSource <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">new</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">EventSource</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token string\">\"/chat\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token number\">3000</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Attempt reconnection after 3 seconds</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>This ensures that SSE messages are properly formatted, displayed in real-time, and automatically reconnected in case of errors.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>4. Advantages and Limitations of SSE</h2>\n<h3>4.1 Advantages</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Ideal for streaming data transmission (e.g., AI chat, log streaming).</li>\n<li>Simple to use, HTTP-based, no additional protocols required.</li>\n<li>Automatic reconnection, suitable for scenarios that do not require bidirectional communication.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4.2 Limitations</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Supports only one-way communication from the server to the client.</li>\n<li>Limited by the number of HTTP connections (browser restrictions on concurrent connections per domain).</li>\n<li>Not reliable in all environments (e.g., some firewalls block persistent connections).</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2>5. Conclusion</h2>\n<p>SSE is an ideal solution for streaming transmission in AI large model chat applications, providing low-latency, efficient real-time experiences. Compared to WebSocket, SSE is more suitable for one-way streaming push of AI-generated content.</p>\n<p>If you need to implement streaming output in AI chat applications, consider using SSE in combination with lightweight web frameworks such as FastAPI to quickly build an efficient AI interaction system.</p>\n<hr>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Server-sent_events\">MDN: Server-Sent Events</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/advanced/custom-response/#streamingresponse\">FastAPI StreamingResponse</a></li>\n</ul>","frontmatter":{"title":"SSE (Server-Sent Events) Protocol and AI Large Model Chat","date":"March 15, 2025","description":"In AI large model chat applications, achieving real-time, streaming responses is crucial for enhancing user experience. Common technical solutions include WebSocket, SSE (Server-Sent Events), and polling. Among them, SSE, as a lightweight one-way communication protocol, is particularly suitable for streaming responses in AI-generated conversations.."}},"previous":{"fields":{"slug":"/mcp/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"What is MCP protocol?"}},"next":null},"pageContext":{"id":"61e49219-b081-5310-97fe-5fcc538d5f66","previousPostId":"2171b696-3589-58cb-aa78-cbd11713dcf1","nextPostId":null}},"staticQueryHashes":["2841359383","3257411868"],"slicesMap":{}}